WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.510 --> 00:00:08.040
- Hi everybody, I'm Maurice Samuels

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:09.990
the Director of the Yale Program

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:11.700
for the Study of Antisemitism.

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:14.890
And it's my great pleasure
to welcome you here today

00:00:14.890 --> 00:00:17.820
to the final installment for this semester

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:21.510
in our special Benjamin and
Barbara Zucker Lecture Series,

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:24.050
dedicated to exploring the connections

00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:26.570
between antisemitism and other forms

00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:28.810
of racism and prejudice.

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:31.330
Today, we're especially
fortunate to have with us

00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:33.440
Terrence L. Johnson.

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:37.460
Terrence is Associate Professor
of Religion and Politics

00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:40.980
in the Department of Government
at Georgetown University,

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:43.340
where he's also an
affiliate faculty member

00:00:43.340 --> 00:00:46.420
of the Department of
African-American studies

00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:49.400
and senior faculty fellow
at the Berkeley Center

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:52.640
for Religion, Peace and World Affairs.

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:53.890
His research interests

00:00:53.890 --> 00:00:56.610
include African-American
political thought,

00:00:56.610 --> 00:01:00.750
American religion and
public life and ethics.

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:01.600
He's the author

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:05.210
of, "We Testify with
Our Lives: How Religion

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:08.220
Transformed Radical
Thought from Black Power

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:09.990
to Black Lives Matter",

00:01:09.990 --> 00:01:11.600
which is about to be published

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:15.550
by Columbia University Press. in 2021.

00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:18.197
He's also the co-author of the forthcoming

00:01:18.197 --> 00:01:21.970
"Blacks and Jews: An
Introduction to a Dialogue"

00:01:21.970 --> 00:01:24.980
which is gonna be published by
Georgetown University Press.

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:27.680
also in 2021.

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:32.197
He's also the author of "Tragic
Soul-Life: W. E. B. Du Bois

00:01:32.197 --> 00:01:35.450
"and the Moral Crisis
Facing American Democracy"

00:01:35.450 --> 00:01:38.470
published by Oxford in 2012.

00:01:38.470 --> 00:01:40.300
His essays have appeared in a number

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:42.210
of edited volumes and journals,

00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:44.687
including the "Journal
of Religious Ethics",

00:01:44.687 --> 00:01:48.090
"Journal of Africana
Religions", "Cross Occurrence"

00:01:48.090 --> 00:01:52.090
and the "Journal of the
Society of Christian Ethics".

00:01:52.090 --> 00:01:55.030
Johnson is also the co-editor
of "The Religious Cultures

00:01:55.030 --> 00:01:59.690
of African and African
Diaspora", people book series,

00:01:59.690 --> 00:02:02.920
which is published by
Duke University Press.

00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:04.610
Now, the way it'll work today

00:02:04.610 --> 00:02:08.180
